      "file_path": "orders/models.py",
      "line_number": 19,
      "line_end": 19,
      "title": "Decimal multiplied by float raises TypeError",
      "description": "total is a Decimal from a DecimalField. apply_discount multiplies it by the float 0.9, and Python raises TypeError for Decimal times float. Every redeem request with the WELCOME10 code returns a server error. No customer can ever get the discount. Multiply by Decimal(\"0.9\") and round the result to two decimal places.",
      "suggested_change": "        self.total = (self.total * Decimal(\"0.9\")).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"))",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "total is a Decimal from a DecimalField. apply_discount multiplies it by the float 0.9, and Python raises TypeError for Decimal times float.",
