      "title": "CSRF protection disabled on a session-authenticated POST",
      "description": "redeem changes order state and authenticates the user with the session cookie. The csrf_exempt decorator turns off Django's CSRF check for this view. A third-party site can make a logged-in user's browser redeem a code on that user's orders. The impact is limited because the only effect is a discount. Remove csrf_exempt and have clients send the CSRF token with the request.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:python.django.security.audit.csrf-exempt.no-csrf-exempt",
